Subject: [PATCH] venus: destroy the device's object mutex after its objects

vkr_device_destroy destroyed dev->object_mutex before it destroyed the objects that the device
still tracks, and each vkr_device_object_destroy ends with vkr_device_remove_object, which locks
that mutex. glibc lets a destroyed mutex be locked; bionic aborts ("FORTIFY:
pthread_mutex_lock called on a destroyed mutex"). So on Android every render server whose
client left with live objects (a game ended or killed, a context made fatal) ended with SIGABRT
and a tombstone instead of a clean exit.

Destroy the mutex after the objects.

---
--- a/src/venus/vkr_device.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_device.c
@@ -369,13 +369,14 @@
          vkr_log("vkDeviceWaitIdle(%p) failed(%d)", dev, (int32_t)result);
    }
 
-   mtx_destroy(&dev->object_mutex);
-
    if (!list_is_empty(&dev->objects)) {
       list_for_each_entry_safe (struct vkr_object, obj, &dev->objects, track_head)
          vkr_device_object_destroy(ctx, dev, obj);
    }
 
+   /* after the objects: each one's removal locks it */
+   mtx_destroy(&dev->object_mutex);
+
    list_for_each_entry_safe (struct vkr_queue, queue, &dev->queues, base.track_head)
       vkr_queue_destroy(ctx, queue);
 
